{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4720",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to bind to Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, both of which are subunits of the Nadh dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) complex, and this complex is associated with Ndufs2. The evidence suggests that Metformin interacts with components of the complex involved in electron transport, which is a critical pathway in cellular respiration. This interaction may modulate the activity of Ndufs2, potentially affecting mitochondrial function. The high scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and robust relationship between Metformin and Ndufs2, suggesting that Metformin's effects on Ndufs2 are mediated through its interaction with these subunits. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition of a key component of the electron transport chain, which could have implications for energy production and cellular homeostasis. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Metformin and Ndufs2, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the precise role of these interactions in disease processes.",
